What is the importance of DevOps in the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)?
 DevOps is important in the SDLC because it integrates development and operations into a continuous lifecycle. 
It enables faster releases through CI/CD, improves quality with automated testing and monitoring, and fosters collaboration 
by breaking down silos. By emphasizing automation, shared ownership, and continuous feedback, DevOps ensures software is delivered reliably, 
securely, and at scale — aligning technical outcomes with business goals.
